      "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn `python/sglang/srt/entrypoints/http_request_decompression.py`, `RequestDecompressionMiddleware.__call__` reassembles incoming compressed ASGI `http.request` chunks on the asyncio event loop before dispatching `_zstd_decompress` to a worker thread:\n\n```python\nbody = b\"\"\nmore_body = True\nwhile more_body:\n    message = await receive()\n    if message[\"type\"] != \"http.request\":\n        return await self.app(scope, receive, send)\n    body += message.get(\"body\", b\"\")\n    more_body = message.get(\"more_body\", False)\n```\n\nBecause `message` is a `dict` (making `message.get(\"body\", b\"\")` have refcount > 1 while stored in `message`), CPython's in-place `bytes` resize optimization cannot trigger on `body += message.get(\"body\", b\"\")`. Every chunk therefore allocates a new `bytes` object and copies the entire prefix accumulated so far, resulting in **$O(K \\cdot B)$ ($O(N^2)$) memory copying directly on the main asyncio event loop** when receiving large zstd-compressed requests (such as base64 multimodal image/video/audio payloads or large batch prompts split across 16 KB–64 KB HTTP chunks).\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Accumulate incoming `http.request` chunks into `chunks = []` and concatenate them in a single pass via `body = b\"\".join(chunks)` once `more_body` is `False`.\n- Add unit tests in `test/registered/cpu/test_request_decompression.py` covering many small chunks, interleaved empty chunks, and verifying single-pass `b\"\".join` without pairwise `+=` concatenation.\n\n### Benchmark (32 MiB zstd-compressed payload across ASGI chunks)\n\n| ASGI Chunk Size | Before (`body += chunk`) | After (`b\"\".join(chunks)`) | Speedup |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 64 KB (512 chunks) | 2.65 s | **0.043 s** | **61.6x faster** |\n| 16 KB (2,048 chunks) | 6.73 s | **0.041 s** | **164.1x faster** |\n\n## Acknowledgments & Related Work\n\nCredits to @Jialin (PR #29684, commit `40594bd38`) for introducing `RequestDecompressionMiddleware`, and to @Snakinya (related open PR #40064 on bounding decompressed size) and @huzhazha (related open PR #36482 on `Content-Encoding` header support).\n\n## Accuracy & Unit Tests\n\n- `pytest test/registered/cpu/test_request_decompression.py`: **10 passed**.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:warning: [Run #41556911230](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41556911230)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:warning: [Run #41556911177](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41556911177)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:warning: [Run #41556911291](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41556911291)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
